oma/kiowa-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years back to 1951, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 10 grids April to May came in under 90% of normal in 39 of them. In 2025 that middle ran 238% of normal in March to April but just 21% in January to February. So far in 2026 it shows 28% in February to March and 46% in April to May. May to June is the wettest pair at 8.19 inches of normal, and January to February the driest at 1.97.</p>"}
